<title>GERMANY: Linde gets 100 mln dmk Indian contract.</title>
<headline>Linde gets 100 mln dmk Indian contract.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany engineering group Linde AG said on Thursday it had won a contract worth around 100 million marks from Bombay-based Reliance Petroleum Ltd to build a hydrogen production plant.</p>
<p>In a statement, Linde said the facility would be the largest of its kind ever built in India.</p>
<p>The plant is due to begin operations at the end of 1998.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
